With variable-sized objects, if decay causes SIZE candidates to include smaller objects, each eviction frees fewer bytes → more cascading evictions needed → massive amplification.

**Root cause**: decay applied to the SIZE source picks smaller objects from deeper in size buckets, requiring more eviction rounds per insertion. This cascades multiplicatively.

**Solution**: Disable decay for the SIZE source — it should always select the absolute largest objects for efficient eviction.

